(ZERO-TRUST CYBERSECURITY INFRASTRUCTURE DOSSIER) '
() '
(Classification: Enterprise Security Operations | Doc Ref: SEC-) '
(ENG-774) '
() '
(1. ZERO-TRUST PERIMETER AND IDENTITY ATTESTATION) '
() '
(Traditional castle-and-moat perimeter security is fundamentally) '
(incapable of neutralizing insider threats, credential compromise,) '
(and lateral network traversal. This architecture mandates zero-trust) '
(verification: every request, whether originating inside or outside) '
(the corporate network, must be explicitly authenticated, authorized,) '
(and encrypted.) '
() '
(Workload identity attestation is enforced through short-lived) '
(cryptographic tokens issued via OpenID Connect \(OIDC\) integrated) '
(with hardware TPM 2.0 chips on host nodes. Context-aware access) '
(policies evaluate device posture, geographic anomaly scores, and) '
(endpoint threat telemetry before granting transient access rights.) '
() '
(2. MUTUAL TLS \(mTLS\) ENCRYPTION AND SERVICE-TO-SERVICE AUTH) '
() '
(All intra-cluster and inter-cluster traffic is encrypted using TLS) '
(1.3 with ChaCha20-Poly1305 and AES-256-GCM cipher suites. Ephemeral) '
(client and server certificates are rotated automatically every 24) '
(hours via automated service mesh sidecars, eliminating risks) '
(associated with stale credentials.) '
() '
ET

endstream
endobj
