(3. CRYPTOGRAPHIC ROOT OF TRUST AND HSM KEY LIFECYCLE) '
() '
(All primary cryptographic keys, master certificate authorities, and) '
(database encryption keys are generated and stored within FIPS 140-3) '
(Level 3 validated Hardware Security Modules \(HSMs\). Key material) '
(never leaves the secure cryptographic boundary in plaintext.) '
() '
(Key rotation schedules are strictly automated: root master keys) '
(rotate every 365 days; intermediate signing keys rotate every 90) '
(days; data encryption keys \(DEKs\) are envelope-encrypted by Key) '
(Encryption Keys \(KEKs\) and rotated per customer data boundary.) '
() '
(4. RUNTIME CONTAINER DEFENSE AND EPBF SECURITY OBSERVABILITY) '
() '
(Runtime security monitoring leverages eBPF probes in the Linux) '
(kernel to intercept system calls \(e.g., execve, connect, ptrace\) in) '
(real time. Anomalous binary execution, unauthorized socket binding,) '
(or file integrity modifications trigger immediate container) '
(isolation and forensic memory snapshots.) '
() '
ET

endstream
endobj
